{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>It is better to dwell on a corner of a roof</b> — for when the house falls the corner remains, because it is the strength of the building, and it is good to dwell on it alone, to bear the wind rather than endure a contentious wife." "<b>A companion</b> — a noun, for the adjective is milra, meaning 'and a house of companionship,' meaning that he would have a house to join with her."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:56.539039816Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}